# macOS helpers

Follow the capture and selection-lookup invariants in root `AGENTS.md`, `internal/capture/macos/README.md`, and `docs/architecture.md`. Treat each Swift helper and its Go adapter as one process boundary, and keep all non-Darwin stubs (`platform_source_stub.go`, `internal/capture/macos/adapter_stub.go`, `internal/selection/runner_other.go`) building.

- Capture (`call-analyzer-capture` + `internal/capture/macos`): `CaptureDefaults.chunkSeconds` and `platform_source_darwin.go` use 2-second 16 kHz mono WAV chunks; Go assembles utterance windows in `internal/service/capture_pipeline.go`. Helper commands are `list`, `capture`, and `stop` (`capture` requires `--bundle-id` and `--spool`).
- Selection lookup (`call-analyzer-lookup` + `internal/selection`): `helperEnvironment` must strip `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` and `SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY` before starting the `LSUIElement` helper. JSON-line requests are `lookup`, `add`, and `save`. Never log selection text or expose it in `AppSnapshot`.
- `swift build` works with Command Line Tools for both packages. `swift test` requires full Xcode; `scripts/verify.sh` builds both Swift packages on macOS and handles the XCTest skip when full Xcode is absent.
